                <pb facs="0387" n="281" xml:id="pg281"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-05-09"><hi rendition="#italic">May 9,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Root inquires whether the imperial edict constitutes a practical
                    nullification of the declaration of 1898 that an Englishman shall be
                    inspector-general.)</p>
            </div>
